# McRogueFace ThreadSanitizer Suppression File
#
# Only third-party code that TSan cannot see synchronise. An engine frame never
# belongs here: a race whose accesses are in src/ is a bug.
#
# Mesa's threaded-context worker (thread "gdrv0", started on first render) and the
# main thread share driver-owned buffers. The driver isn't instrumented, so its
# futex/atomic sync is invisible and every GL-drawing test reports a memcpy race
# inside iris_dri.so. Mesa >= 24 ships the drivers as libgallium-*.so; that line is
# untested here (this machine has iris_dri.so).
race:*_dri.so
race:libgallium*.so
#
# SFML 2.6: Shader::isAvailable() takes its own mutex, then the transient-context
# mutex; another path takes them in the other order. Both are taken on the main
# thread (only the main thread touches GL), so the inversion cannot deadlock.
deadlock:sf::priv::GlContext::acquireTransientContext
